From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:02:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] soc: mediatek: vcp: Build the MT6878 VCP host driver,
 numbered starts, start diagnostics

EXPERIMENTAL: whether the VCP firmware comes up on the phone is still
open; no video codec uses it yet.

- Wire the reduced VCP host port into the build
  (CONFIG_MTK_TINYSYS_VCP_SUPPORT): 34-bit DMA mask behind the IOMMU,
  build fixes for 7.2.
- A start is one numbered attempt with a state: vcp_register_feature()
  waits for the ready message of that attempt (ready_timeout_ms) and
  returns 0 only when the firmware is ready; on failure everything is put
  back and the failing step is named in the log and in vcp_status.
- The start follows a fixed order step by step (clocks, domain, access
  control call, interrupts, the shared memory registers, the core clock
  mux switch, reset release); while the ready message is awaited the
  core is sampled (status, reset register, PC/LR/SP) to tell the cause of
  a failed start; vcp_request sends a first status request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
